{
  "title": "ISic001373. Fragmentary funerary inscription",
  "body": "<div id=\"editions\"><div class=\"attribution\">Text encoding: Jonathan Prag; edition source: <a href=\"https://www.zotero.org/groups/382445/items/Q2SBPG9F\">https://www.zotero.org/groups/382445/items/Q2SBPG9F</a></div><div id=\"edition-interpretive\" lang=\"grc\">  <div class=\"textpart\" lang=\"grc\"><span class=\"ab\" id=\"div-interpretive\">  <a id=\"al1-interpretive\"><!--0--></a><span class=\"linenumber\">1</span><span data-text=\"ἐνθάδε\">ἐνθά[δε]</span>  <span data-text=\"κεῖται\">[κεῖται</span>  <span dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---</span>] <br id=\"al2-interpretive\"><span class=\"linenumber\">2</span>ΞΕΝΑΠΟ[<span dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---</span>] <br id=\"al3-interpretive\"><span class=\"linenumber\">3</span>ΚΟΙ[<span dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---</span>] <br id=\"al4-interpretive\"><span class=\"linenumber\">4</span><span data-text=\"καὶ\">καὶ</span>  <span data-text=\"εἴ\">εἴ</span>  <span data-text=\"τις\">τ[ις]</span>  <span data-text=\"τολμήσει\">[τολμήσει]</span>  <br id=\"al5-interpretive\"><span class=\"linenumber\">5</span><span data-text=\"ἀνῦξαι\">ἀνῦξ[αι</span>  <span dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---</span>] </span></div>  <p class=\"miniapp\"></p></div><div class=\"attribution\">Text encoding: Jonathan Prag; edition source: <a href=\"https://www.zotero.org/groups/382445/items/Q2SBPG9F\">https://www.zotero.org/groups/382445/items/Q2SBPG9F</a></div><div id=\"edition-diplomatic\" lang=\"grc\"><div class=\"textpart\" lang=\"grc\"><span class=\"ab\" id=\"div-diplomatic\"><a id=\"al1-diplomatic\"><!--0--></a><span class=\"linenumber\">1</span><span data-text=\"ἐνθάδε\">ΕΝΘΑ[..</span><span data-text=\"κεῖται\">......</span><span dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---</span>]<br id=\"al2-diplomatic\"><span class=\"linenumber\">2</span>ΞΕΝΑΠΟ[<span dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---</span>]<br id=\"al3-diplomatic\"><span class=\"linenumber\">3</span>ΚΟΙ[<span dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---</span>]<br id=\"al4-diplomatic\"><span class=\"linenumber\">4</span><span data-text=\"καὶ\">ΚΑΙ</span><span data-text=\"εἴ\">ΕΙ</span><span data-text=\"τις\">Τ[..</span><span data-text=\"τολμήσει\">........]</span><br id=\"al5-diplomatic\"><span class=\"linenumber\">5</span><span data-text=\"ἀνῦξαι\">ΑΝΥΞ[..</span><span dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---</span>]</span></div><p class=\"miniapp\"></p></div></div>  <div id=\"facsimile-images\"><h2>Facsimile Images</h2></div>  <div id=\"apparatus\"><h4>Apparatus criticus</h4><ul><li><span><span>Text of Kaibel, after Amico</span></span>; </li><li><span class=\"line 2\">line.2: <span>ΞΕΝΑΠΟ[--- Amico, IG XIV 554; ξενι Πο[--- SGDI 5239; Ξεναό[ρας CIG IV 9513</span></span><br></li><li><span class=\"lines 2-3\">lines.2-3: <span>ἐ]|κοι[μήθη CIG IV 9513</span></span><br></li><li><span class=\"line 4\">line.4: <span>καὶ εἴ τ[ις τολμήσει CIG IV 9513, IG XIV 554; καὶ εἴ τ[ις Amico, SGDI 5239</span></span></li></ul></div>  <div id=\"translation\"><h2>English translation</h2><p class=\"translation-author\"><a href=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5187-5163\">Marta Fogagnolo</a></p>  <p>Here lies … and whoever dares to open ...</p>  </div>  <div id=\"commentary\"><h2>commentary</h2>  <p>Presumably line 2 preserves part of a personal name. The only record from autopsy would seem to be that of Amico. The funerary inscription opens with the traditional formula <span class=\"lang\" lang=\"grc\">ἐνθάδε κεῖται</span> (l. 1). Lines 4–5 contain a curse formula directed against anyone who might violate the tomb (for comparable examples from Catania, see IMusCatania 212 = <a href=\"https://sicily.classics.ox.ac.uk/inscription/ISic000647\" target=\"_blank\">ISic000647</a>; for Christian curse formulas, see Feissel 1980, 464–470).</p>  </div>  <div id=\"bibliography\"><h2>bibliography</h2>  <ul><li> Amico 1741 276 <a href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002186\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002186</a>  </li><li> Kirchhoff 1877 9513 <a href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001250\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001250</a>  </li><li> Kaibel 1890 <a href=\"https://clio.columbia.edu/catalog/6873760\" target=\"_blank\">554</a>  <a href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001072\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001072</a>  </li><li> Hoffmann 1904 5239 <a href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10000817\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10000817</a>  </li></ul>  <ul><li> Feissel 1980 464–470 </li></ul>  </div>  <div id=\"handnote\"> Line 1    Interlineation line 1 to 2    </div><div id=\"license\"> Licensed under a Creative Commons-Attribution 4.0 licence. </div>",
  "divs": [
    {
      "id": "editions",
